 "notes": [
  {
   "html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>The author: “For soba, make the broth just a little stronger.” They don’t give amounts.</li><li><b>Our suggestion (untested):</b> add <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tbsp\" data-a=\"0.5\" data-s=\"0\">½ tbsp</span> more soy sauce and <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tbsp\" data-a=\"0.5\" data-s=\"0\">½ tbsp</span> more mirin, or use <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"ml\" data-a=\"350\" data-s=\"0\">350 ml</span> dashi instead of <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"ml\" data-a=\"400\" data-s=\"0\">400 ml</span>.</li><li>Taste before serving.</li></ul>",
   "title_html": "“A little stronger” for soba"
  },
  {
   "html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>The recipe is written for udon and gives no soba amount or method.</li><li>The <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"mass\" data-u=\"g\" data-a=\"100\" data-s=\"0\">100 g</span> dried soba per serving, the unsalted boil and the cold rinse come from Just One Cookbook’s zaru soba.</li><li>The quick dip back in hot water to warm the rinsed noodles is ours.</li></ul>",
   "title_html": "The noodles"
  },
  {
   "html": "<p>Brands vary. The author’s makes <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"ml\" data-a=\"200\" data-s=\"0\">200 ml</span> of soup per <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tsp\" data-a=\"1\" data-s=\"0\">1 tsp</span>; use a little less of a stronger one and taste at the end.</p>",
   "title_html": "Bouillon strength"
  },
  {
   "html": "<p>Usukuchi is pale but saltier than regular soy sauce — don’t add extra for colour.</p>",
   "title_html": "Light soy sauce"
  },
  {
   "html": "<p>Use only the white and pale green parts, and sear it longer.</p>",
   "title_html": "Regular leek"
  }
 ],
