   "uses_rows": [
    {
     "amount_html": "<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"mass\" data-u=\"g\" data-a=\"100\">100 g</span><span class=\"qalt\"> (<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"mass\" data-u=\"oz\" data-a=\"3.5\" data-alt=\"1\">3½ oz</span>)</span>",
     "name_html": "Japanese leek (naganegi)"
    },
    {
     "amount_html": "<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"count\" data-a=\"2\" data-f=\"sheet|sheets\" data-n=\"1\">2 sheets</span>",
     "name_html": "Fried tofu pouch (aburaage)"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Warm a large frying pan over medium. Add the oil.</li><li>Lay the chicken in <b>skin-side down</b> and wedge the leek into the gaps, everything in one layer.</li></ul>",
   "heat": {
    "label": "medium",
    "label_html": "<span>medium</span>",
    "off": false
   },
   "id": "step-2",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Sear the chicken, leek alongside",
    "diagram": null,
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Chicken in skin-side down, leek in the gaps — one layer.",
      "src": "illustrations/tori-nanban-soba/2-how1.webp?v=d9a17821c7"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/tori-nanban-soba/2.webp?v=6bea1a3a8c",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 2,
   "part": null,
   "part_id": null,
   "time": "~5 min",
   "time_html": "<span>~5 min</span>",
   "title": "Sear the chicken, leek alongside",
   "uses_rows": [
    {
     "amount_html": "<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tsp\" data-a=\"1\">1 tsp</span>",
     "name_html": "Neutral oil"
    },
    {
     "amount_html": "<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"mass\" data-u=\"g\" data-a=\"250\">250 g</span><span class=\"qalt\"> (<span class=\"q\" data-k=\"mass\" data-u=\"lb\" data-a=\"0.5\" data-alt=\"1\">½ lb</span>)</span>",
     "name_html": "Boneless chicken thigh, skin on"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Leave the chicken alone until the skin is golden, then turn it and sear the other side until it’s cooked through.</li><li>Roll the leek now and then so it chars all the way round.</li><li>If the browned bits in the pan have burned black, lift out the chicken and leek and wipe the pan.</li></ul>",
   "heat": {
    "label": "medium",
    "label_html": "<span>medium</span>",
    "off": false
   },
   "id": "step-3",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Turn and char",
    "diagram": null,
    "how": [
     {
      "caption": "Leave it until the skin is golden, then turn; roll the leek so it chars all round.",
      "src": "illustrations/tori-nanban-soba/3-how1.webp?v=ef7e39619c"
     }
    ],
    "illustration": null,
    "photo": null,
    "result": "illustrations/tori-nanban-soba/3.webp?v=e05456b1f1",
    "svg_fallback": null
   },
   "n": 3,
   "part": null,
   "part_id": null,
   "time": "~3–5 min",
   "time_html": "<span>~3–5 min</span>",
   "title": "Turn and char",
   "uses_rows": []
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Pour in the dashi and bring it to a boil.</li><li>Turn the heat to low and add:<ul class=\"ing two-col\"><li>chicken bouillon powder <span class=\"amt\"><span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tsp\" data-a=\"1\">1 tsp</span></span></li><li>light soy sauce (usukuchi) <span class=\"amt\"><span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tbsp\" data-a=\"1\">1 tbsp</span> — or regular Japanese soy sauce</span></li><li>sake <span class=\"amt\"><span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tbsp\" data-a=\"1\">1 tbsp</span></span></li><li>mirin <span class=\"amt\"><span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tbsp\" data-a=\"1\">1 tbsp</span></span></li><li>salt <span class=\"amt\"><span class=\"q\" data-k=\"vol\" data-u=\"tsp\" data-a=\"0.125\">⅛ tsp</span></span></li></ul></li></ul>",
   "heat": {
    "label": "low",
    "label_html": "<span>low</span>",
    "off": false
   },
   "id": "step-4",
   "images": {
    "alt": "Dashi and seasoning",
